% authority congress: glevo:usaCongress
% jurisdiction us: glevo:usa
a person is an infringer.

rule ps1:
a party is forbidden that the party uses a work if
    the work is a work protected by copyright
    and a copyright owner owns the copyright in the work
    and the copyright owner is not the same person as the party.

rule ps2_tblock1:
a party is obliged that statutory damages of between $250 and "$10,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and a copyright owner elects statutory damages
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated
    and it is not the case that
        the person is an infringer
        and the copyright owner sustains the burden of proof
        and the party infringed wilfully
        and the prohibition of the party that the party uses the work is violated.

rule ps3_tblock1:
a party is obliged that increased statutory damages of between $250 and "$50,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and a second party sustains the burden of proof
    and the party infringed wilfully
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated
    and it is not the case that
        the person is an infringer
        and the party sustains the burden of proof
        and it is not the case that the party infringed wilfully
        and the prohibition of the party that the party uses the work is violated.

rule ps4_tblock1:
a party is obliged that reduced statutory damages of between $100 and "$10,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and the party sustains the burden of proof
    and it is not the case that the party infringed wilfully
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated.

rule ps2_tblock2:
a party is obliged that statutory damages of between $500 and "$20,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and a copyright owner claims statutory damages
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated
    and it is not the case that
        the person is an infringer
        and the copyright owner sustains the burden of proof
        and the party infringed wilfully
        and the prohibition of the party that the party uses the work is violated.

rule ps3_tblock2:
a party is obliged that increased statutory damages of between $500 and "$100,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and a second party sustains the burden of proof
    and the party infringed wilfully
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated
    and it is not the case that
        the person is an infringer
        and the party sustains the burden of proof
        and it is not the case that the party infringed wilfully
        and the prohibition of the party that the party uses the work is violated.

rule ps4_tblock2:
a party is obliged that reduced statutory damages of between $200 and "$20,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and the party sustains the burden of proof
    and it is not the case that the party infringed wilfully
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated.

rule ps2_tblock3:
a party is obliged that statutory damages of between $750 and "$30,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and a copyright owner claims statutory damages
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated.

rule ps3_tblock3:
a party is obliged that increased statutory damages of between $750 and "$150,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and a second party sustains the burden of proof
    and the party infringed wilfully
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated.

rule ps4_tblock3:
a party is obliged that reduced statutory damages of between $200 and "$30,000" are paid if
    a person is an infringer
    and the party sustains the burden of proof
    and it is not the case that the party infringed wilfully
    and the prohibition of the party that the party uses a work is violated.

scenario statutory_damages is:
    % 17 USC 504(c)(1): the owner elects statutory damages instead of actual damages.
    novel is a work protected by copyright.
    ann owns the copyright in novel.
    ann is not the same person as ben.
    ben uses novel.
    ann elects statutory damages.
    ann claims statutory damages.
    prohibitions expects answers ["ben is forbidden that ben uses novel"].
    obligations expects answers ["ben is obliged that statutory damages of between $250 and $10,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that statutory damages of between $500 and $20,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that statutory damages of between $750 and $30,000 are paid"].
    violated_obligations expects answers ["the obligation of ben that statutory damages of between $250 and $10,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that statutory damages of between $500 and $20,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that statutory damages of between $750 and $30,000 are paid is violated"].
    violated_prohibitions expects answers ["the prohibition of ben that ben uses novel is violated"].
    breaches expects answers ["ben is in breach"].

scenario wilful_infringement is:
    % 17 USC 504(c)(2): the owner proves the infringement was wilful.
    novel is a work protected by copyright.
    ann owns the copyright in novel.
    ann is not the same person as ben.
    ben uses novel.
    ann elects statutory damages.
    ann claims statutory damages.
    ann sustains the burden of proof.
    ben infringed wilfully.
    prohibitions expects answers ["ben is forbidden that ben uses novel"].
    obligations expects answers ["ben is obliged that statutory damages of between $750 and $30,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that increased statutory damages of between $250 and $50,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that increased statutory damages of between $500 and $100,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that increased statutory damages of between $750 and $150,000 are paid"].
    violated_obligations expects answers ["the obligation of ben that statutory damages of between $750 and $30,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that increased statutory damages of between $250 and $50,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that increased statutory damages of between $500 and $100,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that increased statutory damages of between $750 and $150,000 are paid is violated"].
    violated_prohibitions expects answers ["the prohibition of ben that ben uses novel is violated"].
    breaches expects answers ["ben is in breach"].

scenario innocent_infringement is:
    % 17 USC 504(c)(2): the infringer proves it was not aware that its acts infringed.
    novel is a work protected by copyright.
    ann owns the copyright in novel.
    ann is not the same person as ben.
    ben uses novel.
    ann elects statutory damages.
    ann claims statutory damages.
    ben sustains the burden of proof.
    prohibitions expects answers ["ben is forbidden that ben uses novel"].
    obligations expects answers ["ben is obliged that reduced statutory damages of between $100 and $10,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that reduced statutory damages of between $200 and $20,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that reduced statutory damages of between $200 and $30,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that statutory damages of between $250 and $10,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that statutory damages of between $500 and $20,000 are paid", "ben is obliged that statutory damages of between $750 and $30,000 are paid"].
    violated_obligations expects answers ["the obligation of ben that reduced statutory damages of between $100 and $10,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that reduced statutory damages of between $200 and $20,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that reduced statutory damages of between $200 and $30,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that statutory damages of between $250 and $10,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that statutory damages of between $500 and $20,000 are paid is violated", "the obligation of ben that statutory damages of between $750 and $30,000 are paid is violated"].
    violated_prohibitions expects answers ["the prohibition of ben that ben uses novel is violated"].
    breaches expects answers ["ben is in breach"].

scenario own_work is:
    % The owner using its own work infringes nothing.
    novel is a work protected by copyright.
    ann owns the copyright in novel.
    ann uses novel.
    prohibitions expects answers [].
    obligations expects answers [].
    violated_obligations expects answers [].
    violated_prohibitions expects answers [].
    breaches expects answers [].

query prohibitions is:
    which party is forbidden that which sentence.

query obligations is:
    which party is obliged that which sentence.

query violated_obligations is:
    the obligation of which party that which sentence is violated.

query violated_prohibitions is:
    the prohibition of which party that which sentence is violated.

query breaches is:
    which party is in breach.

